The supplied file DODGY.OPL shows
how to dynamically replace the
procedures in your main program with
new ones from another OPO file.

It uses an undocumented "feature" of
OPL whereby unloading and reloading the
main program forces its procedure list
to be placed "at the back of the queue"

This is not guaranteed to work on
future machines, but if it doesn't then
it would be because OPL worked in a way
that no longer required this procedure
to exist, so no problems there!

Jezar
For the 1994 Psion Developers Conference

